      "type": "text",
      "html": "<h2 style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\"true\">Rows scale with the width</h2>"
    },
    "yui_3_17_2_1_1793705593367_16145": {
      "type": "text",
      "html": "<p style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\"true\">On desktop the smallest a row can be is the container width times 0.0215. A 1400px container gives rows of 30.1px. On phones rows start at a fixed 24px.</p><p style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\"true\">Row height follows the width, so a layout keeps its proportions when the window changes.</p>"
    },
